# Supabase / Leaderboard Rules

Backend is wired via env vars only. The app MUST still run if Supabase is unconfigured.

## Env vars
- Client: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`.
- Migrations (local): `DATABASE_URL` in `.env.local` (never commit).
- Server-only (optional): `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`. NEVER expose to the client.

## Clients
- If env vars are missing, return `null`/no-op and fall back to `localStorage`. Do not crash.

## Validation (shared)
- Use `lib/leaderboardLimits.ts` for caps and `validateScorePayload()` in `POST /api/score`.
- DB enforces the same rules via `scores_insert_allowed()` + RLS (see `supabase/migrations/002_tighten_rls.sql`).

## Score caps (per mode)
- `reaction`: 250 score, level 5
- `memory`: 25000 score, level 200
- `train`: 50000 score, level 200
- `echo`: 15000 score, level 50

## Rate limits
- 15 submissions per player name per hour (all modes)
- 6 per player per mode per hour
- API also limits 20 POSTs/min per IP on `/api/score`

## API routes
- `POST /api/score`: validate → insert → `{ rank }`. Return 400 (bad payload), 429 (rate limit).
- `GET /api/leaderboard?mode=`: top 20 by score desc.

## Migrations
- `npm run db:migrate` runs `supabase/schema.sql` then `supabase/migrations/*.sql` (needs `DATABASE_URL`).

```ts
const validated = validateScorePayload(body, isGameMode);
if (!validated.ok) return NextResponse.json({ error: ... }, { status: 400 });
```
